# Icon buttons

Every new icon-only control gets the shared hover. Do not ship a new icon without it.

- Add class `icon-hover` on the button (or use `button.icon-btn`, which already includes hover).
- Hit target is a circle/pill: `border-radius: 9999px`.
- Center the glyph for real: `display: grid; place-items: center; line-height: 0` on the button, and `display: block` on the SVG (inline SVG baseline will otherwise sit low).
- Hover is a glyph scale + color, not a circular wash and not the lime smash used on text pills. Gate with `@media (hover: hover)` and `:not(:disabled)`.
- Selected (`.is-on`) keeps its rest fill; hover still scales the glyph.

```html
<button type="button" class="icon-hover" aria-label="…">
  <span aria-hidden="true">${someIcon}</span>
</button>
```
